# =============================================================================
# Product — CATEGORY CREATE probes — POST /api/v1/categories (ADMIN)
# =============================================================================
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request below.
#
# Prerequisites (admin persona):
#   Signup admin@devtunde.com with Password123! once, then promote in MySQL:
#     update users set role = 'ROLE_ADMIN' where email = 'admin@devtunde.com';
#
# Notes:
#   - Run top-to-bottom on first use.
#   - All data is FAKE (devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
#   - The automated suite for these endpoints: ProductApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Access tokens expire after 15 MINUTES — re-send the setup requests
#     from the top (they mint fresh captures anyway), then continue.
#   - Response captures are SESSION-SCOPED: closing/reopening this file or VS Code clears them. If a request errors with "No value is resolved" or the URL carries raw template text, re-send the setup requests from the top.
#   - Re-running is SAFE: setup categories are minted fresh via {{$timestamp}}
#     each run. The duplicate probe (13-14) uses a FIXED name on purpose: its
#     conflict target persists across runs, so request 14 409s every time.
#   - Category names are UNIQUE (V6): a taken name returns 409.
#   - Expected codes: 201 created, 400 invalid/missing name, 401 no/garbage
#     token, 403 non-admin caller, 409 duplicate name.
# =============================================================================

@categoryUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/categories
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: signup Devtunde (the admin)
# Expected: 201
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Admin Devtunde",
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031230044"
}

### 2 — Setup: login the admin persona
# Expected: 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 3 — Create a category (fresh name every run)
# Expected: 201 — publicId, name, createdAt, updatedAt
# @name categoryOk
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Beverages {{$timestamp}}"
}

### 4 — No Authorization header
# Expected: 401
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "No Token Category"
}

### 5 — Garbage token
# Expected: 401
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

{
  "name": "Garbage Token Category"
}

### 6 — Setup: signup a regular persona
# Expected: 201 (409 if she already exists — either way the account exists)
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probie Regular",
  "email": "probe.regular@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031110001"
}

### 7 — Setup: login the regular persona
# Expected: 200
# @name regularLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "probe.regular@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 8 — Create as a regular user
# Expected: 403 — category CUD is chain-admin-only (@PreAuthorize)
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{regularLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Nope Category"
}

### 9 — Blank name
# Expected: 400 — field error on "name" (@NotBlank)
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": ""
}

### 10 — Name over 100 characters
# Expected: 400 — field error on "name" (@Size max 100)
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "This category name is far too long to be legal because the validation layer caps names at one hundred characters exactly"
}

### 11 — Missing name field entirely
# Expected: 400 — @NotBlank rejects null
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{}

### 12 — Malformed JSON
# Expected: 400 — "Malformed request body" (HttpMessageNotReadable)
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "name": "Unclosed

### 13 — Second category (categories are a chain vocabulary, so several exist)
# Expected: 201
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Snacks {{$timestamp}}"
}

### 14 — Setup: create the duplicate-probe's FIRST copy
# Expected: 201 on first run; 409 on every later run (name persists) —
# harmless either way: NOTHING chains off this request's capture
# @name clashVocabulary
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Clash Vocabulary"
}

### 14 — Create the SAME name again — the uniqueness contract
# Expected: 409 — "Category already exists" (V6 + service check)
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Clash Vocabulary"
}
